* L54b2: CMPTA - the bench's CMPOD calibrated on TI's TLV1701 model (not TI's model: the user's
* choice in L54b2, "Comportamentale tarato"). The numbers are those measured on the derivative
* models/comparator/tlv1701_ngspice.lib in its circuit (validate_models.py tb_tlv1701,
* prova/tb_ritardi.cir):
*   threshold at -0.4 mV (the model's V_VOS on IN+), the decision a tanh 0.1 mV wide;
*   delays: TI's model 460 ns high-to-low and 574 ns low-to-high at 100 mV of overdrive and a 10k
*   pull-up, 5 ns step (SBOS589D 460 / 560). One pole of 745 ns on the decision and the output
*   switched at half of it give both: with a 10k pull-up and 150 ohm the output crosses 2.5 V at
*   0.458 of the delayed decision, 0.612 tau going in and 0.781 tau coming out (456 / 582 ns
*   for 745 ns). (Two delay lines in its place chattered on a slow ramp with the bench's 20 us
*   step; a sink proportional to the decision crossed 2.5 V at ~1.5 % of it, moving the threshold
*   by ~1 mV: prova/, the earlier versions.)
*   the output 150 ohm when sinking (75 mV at 0.5 mA); 55 uA; CMPOD's supply gate at 2 V.
* Pins as CMPOD: inp inn out vcc gnd (it sinks out when inn > inp - 0.4 mV).
.subckt CMPTA inp inn out vcc gnd
Bu u gnd V = 0.5*(1+tanh((V(inn)-V(inp)-0.4m)/0.1m)) * 0.5*(1+tanh((V(vcc,gnd)-2)/0.1))
R1 u c 1k
C1 c gnd 745p
Bs out gnd I = V(out,gnd)/150 * 0.5*(1+tanh((V(c,gnd)-0.5)/0.02))
Rleak out gnd 1G
Bq vcc gnd I = 55u*(V(vcc,gnd)>1)
.ends
